values ('b1c2d3e4-5f6a-4c91-8d01-2e3f4a5b6c11', 'classical-social-theory', 'Classical Social Theory', 'This course introduces the major questions, texts, and debates that shaped classical social theory. Students study how early sociologists and social theorists explained modernity, capitalism, bureaucracy, religion, urban life, race, gender, social order, conflict, power, and inequality. The course centers Marx, Durkheim, and Weber while also treating Comte, Simmel, Du Bois, Martineau, Gilman, and the Chicago School as essential to understanding the emergence and limits of sociology.');

